      "rule": {
        "type": "unparsed",
        "text": "Completion of the major for either a B.S. or a B.A. in Psychology requires 58 to 67 credits, including 34 to 35 credits in psychology and 24 to 32 credits of courses outside the Department.",
        "reason": "Program-wide credit totals are not a rule type this engine can evaluate."
      },
      "sourceText": "Completion of the major for either a B.S. or a B.A. in Psychology requires 58 to 67 credits. For both degree programs, 34 to 35 credits in psychology to be distributed as follows... In addition to the 34 to 35 credits in psychology, students must also complete 24 to 32 credits of courses outside the Department."
    },
