      "topic": "advising",
      "text": "Students interested in a Psychology major should meet with a Psychology Department Undergraduate Advisor (Room B-109). Additional meetings should be scheduled periodically to review progress toward Department requirements. Students are also strongly encouraged to become research assistants (PSY 273) if planning graduate school."
    },
    {
      "topic": "grading",
      "text": "Psychology courses may be repeated only ONE time. No more than six credits from among PSY 273, PSY 283, PSY 447, and PSY 487 may be taken in one semester."
    },
    {
      "topic": "other",
      "text": "The concentration in Anthropology, Biology, Mathematics, Philosophy, Political Science, or Sociology automatically satisfies the matching outside-course requirement among items 1 to 4 for the B.A. student (for example, the Biology concentration also satisfies item 2). This cross-satisfaction is not modeled."
    },
    {
      "topic": "other",
      "text": "The Psychology Honors Program (not modeled): requires a 3.50 GPA in psychology courses and a 3.20 cumulative GPA to apply at the end of the junior year, a faculty mentor, and a senior thesis via PSY 495 and PSY 496. Conferral requires a cumulative GPA of 3.00 and a 3.50 psychology GPA."
    },
    {
      "topic": "other",
      "text": "Minors of particular interest to Psychology majors: Africana Studies (AFS) and Women's and Gender Studies (WST)."
    }
